<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peace of Szatmár</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1711</span> · Also known as Treaty of Szatmár · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rakoczis-war-of-independence">Rákóczi's War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peace of Szatmár was concluded in April 1711 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> monarchy and the Hungarian insurgents of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii-rakoczi">Francis II Rákóczi</a>, ending the war of independence he had led since 1703. The rebels received an amnesty and the Habsburgs promised to respect the constitution and religious liberties of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, while Rákóczi himself rejected the terms and went into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peace-of-szatmar.jpg" alt="Peace of Szatmár" width="320" height="255" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Österreichisches Staatsarchiv · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Friede_von_Sathmar_1711_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
